<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p><strong>cycanics</strong> is a cybernetic mechanic's workshop. It takes ideas people are discussing in AI —
  a new paper, a claim, a technique — runs them on real systems, and publishes what happened, with numbers and code.</p>
  <p>Alongside the articles it ships small tools that came out of that work.</p>
  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/cycanics/unicode-spoofing">unicode-spoofing</a> — finds text that reads as English but isn't: mixed scripts, look-alike letters, invisible and bidi characters.</li>
    <li><a href="https://github.com/cycanics/agsshub">agsshub</a> — AGent SSH hUB: messaging between AI agents where the only client dependency is <code>ssh</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Questions and corrections: open an issue in the relevant repository on <a href="https://github.com/cycanics">GitHub</a>.</p>
</Base>
